// Root Go workspace.
//
// The shared backend packages live in packages/gointernal. Go's `internal/`
// visibility is module-scoped, so shared code lives in its own module rather
// than an internal/ directory that neither application could import.
//
// apps/api and apps/indexer join this list once they have code; the sync loop
// and HTTP layer are the next milestone.
//
// Foundry and pnpm dependencies are deliberately kept out of Go tooling, and Go
// out of pnpm (monorepo rules).
go 1.27.1

use ./packages/gointernal
